<title>USA: U.S. Nov consumer prices rose 0.3 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. Nov consumer prices rose 0.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Labor Department monthly Consumer Price Index (CPI-U), 1982-84 equals 100:</p>
<p>    Percent Changes:  Seasonally Adj   Unadjusted</p>
<p>    -			   Nov    Oct   Nov96/95</p>
<p> All Items		    0.3    0.3	3.3</p>
<p> -Excluding Food/Energy   0.2    0.2	2.6</p>
<p> Energy			 1.2    0.7	8.1</p>
<p> Food, Drink		  0.3    0.6	4.3</p>
<p> Food			   0.3    0.6	4.4</p>
<p> CPI-Urban Consumers-X  158.6  158.3	N/A</p>
<p>X-Data unadjusted. N/A-Not Available.  </p>
<p>    Percent Changes:  Seasonally Adj   Unadjusted</p>
<p>    -			   Nov    Oct   Nov96/95</p>
<p> Services		     0.2    0.3	3.3</p>
<p> Housing			0.2    0.3	3.0</p>
<p> -Home Fuel Oil	     2.0    6.3     20.8</p>
<p> -Homeowner Costs-Y	 0.3    0.3	2.9</p>
<p> Apparel, Upkeep	    0.5    0.5     -0.2</p>
<p> Transportation	     0.2    0.1	3.9</p>
<p> -Gasoline		    1.8    0.7     11.6</p>
<p> -New Cars		   -0.4   -0.2	1.6</p>
<p>Y-Dec 1982=100 base.  </p>
<p>    Percent Changes:  Seasonally Adj   Unadjusted</p>
<p>    -			   Nov    Oct   Nov96/95</p>
<p> Medical Care		 0.3    0.2	3.1</p>
<p> Commodities		  0.3    0.4	3.1</p>
<p> CPI-W			  0.3    0.3	3.3</p>
<p>CPI-W is the Consumer Price Index for urban wage earners and clerical workers.  </p>
<p>Wall Street economists expected a 0.3 percent rise in November consumer prices. Excluding food and energy, they expected a 0.2 percent increase.</p>
<p>The department said the gain in energy prices in November was the largest since a 3.2 percent increase in April 1996.</p>
<p>It also said natural gas prices surged 3.4 percent in November, posting the sharpest increase since a 4.7 percent rise in October 1982.  </p>
<p>In the first 11 months of this year, the CPI rose at a 3.3 percent seasonally adjusted annual rate compared with a 2.5 percent increase for all of 1995, the department said.</p>
<p>It said airline fares decreased 0.7 percent in November.</p>
</text>
